course: dictionary
lesson: 6945
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. «Paint» can be a thing or an action. As a noun, paint is the coloured liquid itself. As a verb, to paint is to put paint on something. Read the words around it to decide which one it is. «A line painted on its side» shows someone has put paint on the ship.
explain: «Poems paint pictures with words, called imagery.» Here paint does not mean colour at all. A poem has no brush or tin of paint, so the clue is pictures with words. Paint here means to make a picture in your mind using words. Always ask: does the usual meaning fit this sentence? If not, look for another meaning.
explain: Look at the ending too. «Paints» with an s is a noun for a set of colours for art, and «painted» shows something happened in the past. Try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Paint is a coloured liquid that you put on things to colour them or protect them.
fact: To paint means to put paint on something, such as a wall, or to make a picture with paint.
fact: «Paints» are a set of colours for art.
fact: «Paint» can also mean to describe something so clearly that people can picture it, as in «Poems paint pictures with words».
fact: In science, mixing red and yellow paint makes orange, and paint dries as the water in it evaporates.
exercise: «Poems paint pictures with words.» What does paint mean in this sentence? | To put paint on a wall | A coloured liquid in a tin | A set of colours for art | *To make a picture in the mind using words
exercise: «A line painted on its side shows how deep the ship may safely sit.» What does painted mean here? | *Had paint put on it | Cleaned with water | Sailed across the sea | Drawn in pencil
exercise: Nadia says, «The paints are in the art box.» What does paints mean? | To make a picture with words | *A set of colours for art | Brushes for cleaning | A coloured liquid for walls
test: «Workers spray coloured paint marks on the pavement before roadworks.» Why are the paint marks there? | To make the pavement look pretty for the summer | *To show where pipes and cables run, so the diggers do not hit them | To stop the pavement from getting wet | To mix into orange
test: In science class, Ella mixes red paint and yellow paint. What happens? | Purple appears | Black appears | Nothing changes at all | *Orange appears
exam: Which sentence uses paint as a noun, meaning a thing? | «I will paint the fence tomorrow.» | *«She bought a tin of paint for the fence.» | «Poems paint pictures with words.» | «They are painting the hall.»
